From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 20:25:02 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7915: unblock tx after dropping all tokens on
 reset

TX is blocked once token_count gets within MT76_TOKEN_FREE_THR of the
token pool size, and only a tx-free event from the firmware unblocks it
again. Both the full restart and the L1 SER path free every token with
mt76_connac2_tx_token_put() and start over with an empty pool, but leave
the queues blocked. With no tokens outstanding, no tx-free event will
ever arrive, so if tokens had piled up before the reset (as they do
when the firmware stops reporting tx-free while hung) data and
management TX stay stopped on all bands until the driver is reloaded.
With WED the pool is only 4096 tokens, so the threshold is reached more
easily.

Unblock tx after re-initialising the token pool. Also clear
wed_token_count in mt76_connac2_tx_token_put() and wake up tx_wait, so
mt76_wed_offload_enable() doesn't wait for tokens that no longer exist.
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mt76_connac_mac.c | 2 ++
 mt7915/mac.c      | 2 ++
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mt76_connac_mac.c b/mt76_connac_mac.c
index b80bdf0f..a938d49f 100644
--- a/mt76_connac_mac.c
+++ b/mt76_connac_mac.c
@@ -1231,8 +1231,10 @@ void mt76_connac2_tx_token_put(struct mt76_dev *dev)
 		mt76_connac2_txwi_free(dev, txwi, NULL, NULL);
 		dev->token_count--;
 	}
+	dev->wed_token_count = 0;
 	spin_unlock_bh(&dev->token_lock);
 	idr_destroy(&dev->token);
+	wake_up(&dev->tx_wait);
 
 	for (id = 0; id < __MT_MAX_BAND; id++) {
 		struct mt76_phy *phy = dev->phys[id];
diff --git a/mt7915/mac.c b/mt7915/mac.c
index 06cddffa..ff69cf8e 100644
--- a/mt7915/mac.c
+++ b/mt7915/mac.c
@@ -1335,6 +1335,7 @@ mt7915_mac_restart(struct mt7915_dev *dev)
 	/* token reinit */
 	mt76_connac2_tx_token_put(&dev->mt76);
 	idr_init(&dev->mt76.token);
+	mt76_set_tx_blocked(&dev->mt76, false);
 
 	mt7915_dma_reset(dev, true);
 
@@ -1550,6 +1551,7 @@ void mt7915_mac_reset_work(struct work_struct *work)
 
 		mt76_connac2_tx_token_put(&dev->mt76);
 		idr_init(&dev->mt76.token);
+		mt76_set_tx_blocked(&dev->mt76, false);
 
 		mt76_wr(dev, MT_MCU_INT_EVENT, MT_MCU_INT_EVENT_DMA_INIT);
 		mt7915_wait_reset_state(dev, MT_MCU_CMD_RECOVERY_DONE);
